#!args --demo --no-gpu
# the demo without a device (G6e1): --no-gpu sets jfgui_GPU=0, so the view paints its scene through the CPU path (Scene::draw_cpu, a scene
# made without a device); the same script as demo.uis, the same places: the red line through x = 0 (9 px wide, at x 360),
# the blue one through y = 50 (5 px, at y 222); a window selects (blue, grips), Esc clears, the line under the pointer
# orange, the wheel zooms at the pointer, a click picks.  Picking, snapping and highlighting work without a device
wait 600
expect pixel 358 300 #D02020
expect pixel 600 222 #2040C0
expect pixel 385 288 #7C9F8A
drag 300,278 420,306
wait 200
expect pixel 385 288 #618FD7
expect pixel 400 291 #1E64FF
key esc
wait 200
expect pixel 385 288 #7C9F8A
drag 358,300 458,300 middle
wait 200
expect pixel 458 400 #F97F1B
wheel 458,300 120
wait 200
expect pixel 458 400 #F97F1B
expect pixel 600 207 #2040C0
click 458,400
wait 200
move 650,470
wait 200
expect pixel 458 420 #4B53C7
key esc
wait 200
expect pixel 458 420 #D02020
